%% UC-36 — Researcher configures per-group study design in admin portal
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor R as Researcher
    participant A as Admin Portal (Next.js)
    participant B as Backend (Node.js)
    participant M as MongoDB

    R->>A: Open Studies → select study → select group
    A->>B: GET /api/v1/admin/studies/:id  (JWT, admin/researcher role)
    B->>M: studies.findOne({_id})
    M-->>B: study + groups (with current config)
    B-->>A: study detail

    R->>A: Configure per-group toggles:
    Note over R,A: • Restrict activity types → select allowed types<br/>• Restrict cue selection → link to cue pool<br/>• Reminder: enable toggle + optional fixed time (HH:MM)<br/>• Auto-donate habits to community
    R->>A: Save

    A->>B: PATCH /api/v1/admin/studies/:id/groups/:groupId/config<br/>{cueConfig?, activityTypeConfig?, reminderConfig?, autoDonate?}
    B->>M: studies.updateOne({_id}, {$set: {groups: [...]}})
    M-->>B: {matchedCount:1}
    B-->>A: 200 {updated: true}
    A->>R: Group config saved

    Note over R,A: Repeat for other groups (e.g. control group has fewer restrictions)

    Note over B,M: When participant logs in:
    Note over B,M: GET /study-config/me → enrollment → study → group<br/>Returns resolved config to Flutter app
